Version 1.13 brings several improvements and fixes throughout the game:
[list]
[*] Added motion matching system that makes movement much more fluid!;
[*] The motion matching system works for both Chihiro and enemies;
[*] The healing system of the Flask of Cold Flame has been modified, now the amount of Vitality recovered per use is increased according to Chihiro's level of insanity;
[*] The duration system of the Flask of Heat Flame has been modified, now the duration of the effect of recovering Vitality is increased according to Chihiro's level of insanity;
[*] The healing system of the Healing Ointment has been modified, now the amount of Vitality recovered per use represents 10% of Chihiro's maximum Vitality and also removes the Poison status;
[*] Some enemies now have new moves, some attacks have been adjusted so that combat is more fluid and dynamic, and now some enemies can defend and counterattack. Balance adjustments have been made to the status of some enemies;
[*] Some enemies are now immune to certain types of status;
[*] Combat has been improved, enemies can now defend, counterattack or even block a sequence of attacks to avoid StunLock;
[*] The impact effect of combat has been improved and now the bleeding VFX on Chihiro's or enemies' attacks only happens if the attack is effective and the effect has been removed for blocks;
[*] The Boss Inubushi, the Lonely One has been balanced, received new attacks and better movement, in addition to now being immune to bleeding, poison and frozen damage;
[*] The Boss Yoshio, Leader of Kakure has been balanced, he now received new movement logic, reactions to sequences of attacks, and immunity to bleeding and poison;
[*] Inubushi's artificial intelligence has been fixed and now he does not see distant enemies as targets;
[*] A control vibration system has been added (gamepad only);
[*] Achievements have been added;
[*] All enemies' combat animations have been adjusted, with improvements to tracking, hitboxes, and movement speed;
[*] Some sound effects have been improved or had their volumes adjusted;
[*] A considerable reduction in triangle rendering has been made;
[*] Some visual effects have been fixed;
[*] Fixed Bug that caused Bosses' Vitality bar to not go off screen after the player respawns;
[*] Fixed Bug that caused the player to have negative strength after consuming "Invigorating Tea";
[*] The "Rest" option for Flame Lanterns has been removed, now the "rest" function is automatically applied when interacting with the lantern;
[*] Minor logic fixes in UI systems;
[*] Minor collision fixes;
[/list]

Version 1.12 brings some improvements and fixes, in addition to significantly improving performance thanks to the migration to Unreal Engine 5.4.3 (previously it was 5.1.1).
- Fixed errors in the save game that caused an empty fast travel port to be created;
- Fixed some collision errors;
- Lighting improvements;
- Fixed an error that caused Inubushi's Summon to act as a collision for the player;
- New attacks for Inubushi's Summon;
- Fixed an error that caused the new game message to be unclickable;
- Improvements to the rendering system;
- Improvements to Anti Aliasing;
- Improvements to the Inubushi Summon AI;
- Minor performance improvements;
- Minor texture and graphics corrections.

The version fixes some minor bugs that were missing in version 1.10:
- Fixed glitch in fight against Lord Yoshio;
- Fixed glitch that caused the player to not enter the boss fight area correctly;
- Minor text translation fixes;
- Minor audio fixes.

Version 1.1 is focused on fixing the Save game, but it brings some improvements, fixes and a small addition of content.
- Some players still reported bugs when saving and loading the game, a new fix was made and now everything should work correctly; 
[b]**ATTENTION**, the game will still be able to use data saved in previous versions, but if you have seen any save game bug, such as the appearance of an empty fast travel point or loss of dialogue from an NPC, your saved data is in error, so I recommend that you delete the saved file or start a new journey.
In addition, now, when resting at any Flame Lantern, a new save file will be created automatically, serving as AUTO-SAVE.[/b]
- Improvement added to Chihiro's Upgrade system, now it is possible to see which status will be increased and what it affects the player's status, such as health points, strength and base attack power.
- Added a small piece of information about the weapon efficiency scale, now when viewing item details it is possible to read "For: X% | Has X% | Ins: X%" This represents the weapon's attack gain based on its respective attributes.
- Added a new HP bar system, now it is possible to see the amount of damage received before the bar effectively decreases (applicable to the player and bosses).
- Added a message when clicking on "new game" if the player already has an adventure in progress;
- Added a confirmation message to exit the game;
- Added a message/tutorial about inubushi after defeating the boss;
- Added a new mask: "Akiko's Hannya Mask", which can be obtained by defeating the enemy "Flaming Monk" in the "Momiji's Shrine";
- Added a new Katana: "Yoshio's Katana", which can be obtained by defeating the boss "Lord Yoshio". 
- Slightly reduced the brightness of some enemies that had flames on their weapons or bodies;
- Fixed a bug that caused Inubushi to pass through the village entrance more than once, giving the impression that there was something interactable there. (His appearance should have been just a hint about the existence of the boss in the game);
- Fixed a bug that caused Inubushi to walk too much during combat;
- Implemented an Inubushi alert system, now he warns you about hidden items on the map.
- Fixed the volume of Inubushi's footsteps (summoning).
- Fixed/added some translations to English;
- Small corrections to polygons and triangles on the map;
- Small performance improvements.

Version 1.0.8 brings some fixes based on feedback from some players.
- Combat improvements. Combat has now been improved so that Chihiro doesn't easily dodge the target enemy, enemy animations have been improved for all damage received, and Chihiro's movement always stops after attacks;
- Master Hori's initial dialogue has been improved, now the player has the option to ask or not about the Lowlands war, in addition to being able to return to the previous dialogue (Note that the war dialogue is part of his quest, and can be permanently lost if ignored);
- Added auto-save at the entrance to Master Hori's house.
- Added auto-save to every flame lantern;
- Fixed bug that caused the cutscene of Chihiro's entrance to repeat itself in the middle of gameplay;
- Fixed bug that caused Chihiro to return to the starting point of the game if the player died without activating any lantern; - Fixed bug that caused Master Hori's dialogue to reset when loading a saved game;
- Fixed bug that caused Hori to return to his initial position when loading a saved game;
- Minor fixes other than environment bugs;
- Minor improvements to sounds;
- Small performance improvement when loading areas.

Hello everyone!

First of all, thank you very much to everyone who is downloading and playing.

I just posted a video on YouTube about the upcoming updates, bug fixes and improvements.

See it here: https://youtu.be/GVRAAhniig8?si=XQovDCApdWu067fg

Thank you very much to everyone who reported problems and know that I am already working to improve!
You are 10/10.

See you next time!

PS: Some players reported downloading 0bites or without an executable, I don't know what this problem is, it is not with the game files, I am checking with Steam to see what it could be. Thank you all for the report.

